it's been almost a month since the m2  macbook air was released and now that  the hype is settled down let's get real  is it really worth spending way more  money on the 14-inch macbook pro well  today i'm gonna compare everything from  a honest real world perspective and keep  it short and sweet after five years  apple finally redesigned the macbook air  and looks modern but a bit retro at the  same time the 14-inch looks like a  chunkier version of the air but the  extra thickness brings features that can  make a real difference in usability  since i mentioned design let's start  with that the pro looks bigger bulkier  and a bit meaner where the air is thin  and sleek the wet shape is now gone and  personally i'm a bit sad about it since  it was so iconic and it didn't dig into  your wrist for really long typing  sessions but in the real world the new  design is still thin enough not to  matter one weird thing is that online  they look very similar and the specs  seem so close but in the real world you  really notice the weight difference and  the thickness i personally find that the  thicker pro can dig into your wrists and  even though the keyboards have the same  name the airs feels better in my opinion  having a bit more feedback so if you do  a lot of typing you'll prefer the m2 air  one disappointment though with the new  air are the speakers apple made a huge  deal about the quad speakers with  dedicated woofers so we had high  expectations but in reality they got  quieter and with less steer separation  as they got rid of the speaker holes on  the sides and instead they fire towards  the display the 14-inch on the other  hand has the best speakers in any laptop  of this size go ahead and take a listen  [Music]  the difference is shocking with a huge  difference in volume and bass and if  you're somebody that will constantly be  playing them at full blast you will  really enjoy them i know i do now with  that said if i'm being honest if you are  not comparing them side by side the air  speakers still sound good and for most  people they are much better than the  laptop that it will replace with that we  have new ports which your current laptop  may or may not have now i love that  magsafe is back on both of these and on  the air that means that the two  thunderbolt ports are free to use at any  time now yes the 14-inch has one more  thunderbolt and it's more powerful as  well as hdmi and a card reader so if  yours has that now i would track how  often you use those things now for me  most of the time i just use usb type c  and even though dongles suck you should  really ask yourself is it really worth  spending the extra cash to have them  built in instead of buying a cheap  multi-adapter i'll link this one in the  description it's been working great and  i just keep it in my laptop bag now as  for the webcams based on specs they seem  the same being 1080p but we definitely  noticed a difference this is the new  1080p webcam in the m2 macbook air now  it did get a lot better compared to the  720p but the 14 inch macbook pro that  also has a 1080p webcam has less noise a  bit more detail so i think it must be  just the camera module that apple is  using after webcams now is a really good  time to talk about fan noise or lack  thereof if you're somebody who  constantly does zoom meetings and your  current laptop might get annoying  because after a while the fans will spin  up and keep it cool as it processes that  video feed which was a huge issue with  the intel macbook air and that also  impacted audio quality the m2 air is  fanless so it is silent but if you might  be worried about the 14-inch pro because  it does have dual fans thankfully for  most tasks the fans are literally turned  off thanks to apple silicon being very  efficient and since the heat pipes pull  away heat from the processors even if  the fans are off now if you're doing  tough tasks yes they will spin up but  they are still very quiet some people  have mentioned that the m2 air's bottom  case can get really hot with extended  loads and that is true the 14 inch  exhausts the heat upwards away from you  but the fanless m2 air's bottom case can  reach 47 degrees celsius since the heat  is literally trapped in there and up to  108 degrees celsius internally which is  much hotter than the 14 inch if you're  wondering how this impacts performance  without a fan well in our detailed  testing we found that it can lose 17 of  its performance after about 10 minutes  and that is just with cpu tasks as far  as graphics the performance loss can be  over 26  and if you're loading both up at the  same time it could be even more than  that so if you're pushing your mac hard  and you're loading up the cpu and the  graphics the pro is the way to go but if  you need to save some cash and you want  a thin and light design a thin laptop  cooler can make a surprising difference  just by itself i'll go ahead and link  the cooler and the full video in the  description so what about performance  especially if the tasks you do don't  completely max up the cpu for a long  time well this is the reason why most  people would buy the 14-inch pro instead  of the air and it might be the biggest  reason why you're considering it well i  want to challenge you a little bit and  also give you some more info i just want  you to take a second and ask yourself  how much performance do you really need  first off the 2 000 14 inch macbook pro  is the double bin version meaning to get  the full m1 pro chip it costs at least 2  300 and second even the base m2 ear  already beats out even the previous best  16-inch macbook pro in many tasks and  absolutely wipes the floor with the  intel macbook airs in the real world the  air has more than enough performance for  most people even for difficult tasks but  i do have to add that we are using a 512  gigabyte ssd model of the air because  the base 256 gigabyte has a slow ssd  that will not only slow down transfers  but your whole machine if you are  multitasking and doing productive work  now the m2 chip sounds like it could be  better than the m1 pro and it actually  can for a few tasks which i'll mention  but the base 14-inch has six performance  cores two more than the air because of  that the multi-core score isn't that  much higher with the difference of only  eleven percent and this test shows a lot  of various computing tasks so most won't  even notice it in the real world as for  single core the m2 beats out the 14 inch  by nine percent because of its faster  clock speeds which also gives it a good  advantage in web-based application  performance but once again both are so  fast that you probably won't notice what  you will notice though is the difference  in battery life apple specs show that  the m2 air only gets one extra hour of  battery life with the fine print showing  that it's based on video playback but  that's not the truth for real world use  we found that for mixed use the battery  life is worse and a bigger difference  between them and for top tasks the  difference is even greater since the 14  inch can use a lot more power adding on  to that if you use low power mode both  laptops are still very fast but the m2  air can last up to 15 hours because it  will only use 2 watts for the cpu and  1.5 for the graphics that is because it  has 4 efficiency cores and there are new  ones that are much more powerful while  being more efficient now the 14 inch  pro's battery life doesn't improve too  much because it has to keep using the  performance cores as it only has two  efficiency cords that are much worse so  the cpu actually uses about 15 watts  compared to an average of two and using  that mode on the m2 air results in the  machine running super cool and the  bottom not heating up at all so if you  really care about battery life the  macbook air is the clear choice check  out the video if you want to get a lot  more info now when you do need full  performance for more than 10 minutes the  stock m2 air loses by about 30 in cpu  and for graphics by more than double  because the stock macbook air throttles  a lot after just four to five minutes  now if you use the cooling solution that  we showed them to air won't throttle but  it's still a 63 difference which is  massive and spending an extra hundred  dollars for better graphics is mostly a  waste in our testing so if you're doing  graphics heavy tasks like gaming or  productivity tasks that rely on graphics  this is where the 14-inch pro really  starts to stand out and combining both  can make a slightly more pricey 14-inch  if spec the same ending up being more  than twice as fast and a much better  machine to have but let's get real most  of you wanting the air probably won't be  working on raw footage but you're gonna  be using it for web browsing and some  light productivity and maybe some normal  creative work here the differences  aren't massive with the 14 inch only  being slightly faster for photography  and since both are so fast compared to  old intel macbooks in the real world i  had no complaints especially with the 16  gigabyte macbook air which is the one to  get if you're going to be doing  productive tasks and even for things  like compiling code the air can keep up  very well and for simple 4k video  editing with effects it can actually  beat out the 14-inch using the latest  version of davinci resolve which is now  fully optimized for the m2 chip so i  would say that there is only a small  group of people who really need the  extra power of the 14 inch pro but when  you need it like for extended 100 loads  especially with graphics you really need  it and with that comes the mini led xdr  display that is capable of hitting up to  1600 nits instead of 500. now for normal  use you don't really notice a difference  but when it comes time for hdr either  viewing or editing the 14 inch gives you  a much better experience with really  great contrast and brightness that the  m2 air simply cannot achieve as well as  120hz pro motion for super smooth  scrolling which to be honest i didn't  notice as much as i do on my iphone and  also being able to play games at above  60 fps personally unless you know that  you want or need many of the benefits  that the 14 inch provides that we talked  about i think that the air is a great  machine and it is much more pleasant for  taking on the go seriously it's a big  difference but if you don't mind the  size and you can't afford it you do get  a lot more bang for the buck with the 14  inch macbook pro especially if you buy  it discounted on amazon i'll go ahead  and leave the best deals down in the  video description go ahead and check out  one of those must watch videos right  over there especially if you want to buy  an m2 macbook air and click above to  subscribe if this video brought you some  value this has been max max tech and i  will see you in the next video  [Music]

